<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53245" body-key="">*<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάρ</span></b>  (A), a word of uncertain gender, nom. form,
		and meaning, typifying what is worthless, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίω δέ
			μιν ἐν κᾰρὸς αἴσῃ</span> I value him at <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α . . </span>'<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>s worth</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.378
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρός</span> is variously expld.
			by <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
			</span></i> Byz. etc. ap. Sch., e.g.as 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κηρός</span>
			 or as pr.n. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καρός</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάρα, ἐπὶ κάρ</span>
			
			<i>head</i>-long (nisi junctim scrib.), <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.392
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὰ κάρ</span>
			<i>upwards</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.79
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
